MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo Show 8 feels useful because its larger screen would add convenient smart-home controls alongside my Fire TV and security devices.",
    "The smart plug offers a concrete next step: automating a lamp with the Alexa-capable devices I already use. Indoor cameras also fit my monitoring interests, although I do not currently need three more."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Another Fire TV Stick adds little when I already have a 4K Stick and a Fire TV television; sharing the same family does not make it a useful addition.",
    "Voice-only speakers do not fill a clear need when my remote already provides Alexa access. The tablet and AirPods also lack a clear connection to what I am currently trying to do."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Fire TV purchases seem to have been taken as interest in almost any Amazon device, while I care more about the specific function it adds.",
    "My interest in connected home devices seems to have been stretched into interest in multiple speakers and starter bundles, even when their functions overlap with what I have."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "What I already own matters: a recommendation needs to add a useful capability or address a gap, rather than repeat an existing function.",
    "Interest does not always mean I would buy now. I would choose the Show 8 over the Show 5, start with a smart plug rather than a speaker-and-bulb bundle, and wait for a specific coverage need before adding cameras."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my interest in connected home equipment, but treated shared branding and related devices as stronger reasons to buy than practical additions to my current setup."
}
